Package: hd-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, systemd, hd-base (>= 1.91)
Suggests: hd-dashboard
Conflicts: hd-report
Replaces: hd-report
Provides: hd-report
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian agent for the dashboard
 Sends the state of the system to the hyprdebian dashboard of hd-dashboard
 every 15 minutes: the HyprDebian and Debian versions, the kernel, the state
 of Secure Boot, the load, the memory, the ZFS pools, the mdadm arrays, the
 failed units, the pending upgrades and reboots, the last snapshot of hd-up,
 the timers and what hd-harden of hd-base hardened. The system only makes
 outgoing connections.
 .
 It also runs the jobs the dashboard hands out in its reply, made by
 hd-manager: each job is one command, like upgrade, which runs hd-up
 --unattended at the time of the job. A job only runs when it is signed by
 one of the manager_keys in the key hd-agent of /etc/hyprdebian/config.json;
 without them, no job runs.
 .
 The URL of the dashboard is the key hd-agent in
 /etc/hyprdebian/config.json; the token of the system is generated on the
 first installation in /etc/hyprdebian/hd-agent/token. Installing the
 package enables hd-agent.timer.
 .
 It replaces hd-report: installing it removes hd-report and takes over its
 token, its settings and the enabled state of hd-report.timer.
